how_its_made:
this project uses:
(a lot of kotlin)
 - the web3auth kotlin sdk, for abstracting the wallet inside of our application;
 - ens for our off-chain resolver, to provide every address with their own free ens; 
- kinto, where we allow only kyc'd wallets to transact, as for the case of banking in more regulated economies;
-  blockscout, to fetch the data from kinto readable methods;
- pyth for randomness. we have also implemented chainlink vrf for randomness, as well as flow.
